Title: CI: rebuild and commit bootstrap binary when Go source changes merge to main
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: haduong
Closed: done

--- log ---
2026-05-05T00:00Z haduong created

2026-05-05T14:19Z claude closed — done
--- body ---
`tickets/tools/go/erg` is the pre-built binary that `erg update` fetches
from GitHub raw and that `erg init` ships to new projects. It must stay
in sync with the source in `tickets/tools/go/*.go`.

Today there is no automated gate. After 11 PRs across two raids added
`check`, `new`, `log`, `archive`, and other improvements, the committed
binary remained at the PR #37 state. Users running `erg update` got
the same stale binary back — the update path was silently broken.

**Desired behaviour:**

A CI workflow (`.github/workflows/rebuild-binary.yml`) triggers on
push to `main` when any of these paths change:

```
tickets/tools/go/*.go
tickets/tools/go/go.mod
tickets/tools/go/go.sum
```

The workflow:
1. Runs `go build -ldflags "-X main.buildDate=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)" -o tickets/tools/go/erg .` inside `tickets/tools/go/`
2. Checks whether the binary changed (`git diff --exit-code tickets/tools/go/erg`).
3. If changed: commits it directly to main with message
   `chore: rebuild bootstrap binary [skip ci]` and pushes.
4. If unchanged: exits 0 silently.

The `[skip ci]` tag prevents the commit from re-triggering the workflow.

**Alternative considered:** require a human to run `make rebuild-binary`
and include the binary in every code PR. Rejected — it will be forgotten
(as demonstrated twice already).

**Implementation notes:**

- Use `actions/checkout` with `persist-credentials: true` so the push step works.
- The workflow needs write permission to `contents`.
- Build target: `linux/amd64` (GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-latest`).
- If cross-platform binaries are needed in the future, extend this ticket.
- No new Makefile targets needed — the workflow calls `go build` directly.
